From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:14:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Gui: an absolute camera placement stops a running view
 animation (issue 038)

FixedTimeAnimation turns and moves the camera relatively to its previous
step. A camera placed absolutely while it still ran (View3DInventorViewer::
applyCameraState = Python setCamera, Std_FreezeViews, the TempoVis camera
restore after a sketch, BIM section views; setViewDirection; Python
viewDefaultOrientation) was then turned further about the animation's old
rotation centre: e.g. opening a sketch and closing it at once left the view
about 55 degrees turned and 50 mm off the restored camera.

These placements now stop the running animation first, as
NavigationStyle::setCameraOrientation and translateCamera already do before
their own placement; moveCameraTo (Python viewPosition) states it too.
Relative changes (zoom, pan, rotate left/right, orbit) still combine with a
running animation as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Gui/View3DInventorViewer.cpp | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/Gui/View3DPy.cpp             |  5 +++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/View3DInventorViewer.cpp b/src/Gui/View3DInventorViewer.cpp
index c8d272d..4aa7b59 100644
--- a/src/Gui/View3DInventorViewer.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/View3DInventorViewer.cpp
@@ -3657,6 +3657,11 @@ void View3DInventorViewer::setViewDirection(SbVec3f dir)
     if (!navigation) {
         return;
     }
+    // An absolute placement replaces a view animation that still runs (as setCameraOrientation and
+    // translateCamera stop it before their own): FixedTimeAnimation turns and moves the camera
+    // relatively to its previous step, so left running it would turn this new pose about its own
+    // old rotation centre (e.g. a saved view restored during the animated turn to a sketch).
+    navigation->stopAnimating();
     navigation->setCameraOrientationValue(
         getCamera(),
         SbRotation(SbVec3f(0, 0, -1), dir),
@@ -4260,6 +4265,14 @@ bool View3DInventorViewer::applyCameraState(const SoCamera& sourceCamera)
         return false;
     }
 
+    // An absolute placement replaces a view animation that still runs (as setCameraOrientation and
+    // translateCamera stop it before their own): FixedTimeAnimation turns and moves the camera
+    // relatively to its previous step, so left running it would turn this new pose about its own
+    // old rotation centre (e.g. a saved view restored during the animated turn to a sketch).
+    if (navigation) {
+        navigation->stopAnimating();
+    }
+
     if (sourceCamera.getTypeId() != targetCamera->getTypeId()) {
         setCameraType(sourceCamera.getTypeId());
         targetCamera = getCamera();
@@ -4318,6 +4331,12 @@ void View3DInventorViewer::moveCameraTo(const SbRotation& orientation, const SbV
         return;
     }
 
+    // An absolute placement replaces a view animation that still runs (as setCameraOrientation and
+    // translateCamera stop it before their own): FixedTimeAnimation turns and moves the camera
+    // relatively to its previous step, so left running it would turn this new pose about its own
+    // old rotation centre (e.g. a saved view restored during the animated turn to a sketch).
+    navigation->stopAnimating();
+
     if (isAnimationEnabled()) {
         startAnimation(
             orientation,
diff --git a/src/Gui/View3DPy.cpp b/src/Gui/View3DPy.cpp
index 03bed77..877d9f8 100644
--- a/src/Gui/View3DPy.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/View3DPy.cpp
@@ -722,6 +722,11 @@ Py::Object View3DInventorPy::viewDefaultOrientation(const Py::Tuple& args)
             return Py::None();
         }
 
+        // An absolute placement (orientation above, height and position below): a view animation
+        // still running would go on turning this pose about its old rotation centre, see
+        // View3DInventorViewer::applyCameraState
+        navigation->stopAnimating();
+
         if (scale < 0.0) {
             ParameterGrp::handle hGrp = App::GetApplication().GetParameterGroupByPath(
                 "User parameter:BaseApp/Preferences/View"
